[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Bounded affine behavioral-source preparation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-BEHAVIOR-AFFINE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Prepare finite affine voltage and current B-source relations
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated frontend shall retain B-source output polarity, quantity, lexical scope and expression ranges, and shall prepare a finite affine form over node-voltage references and existing scalar parameter evaluation. Admitted operators are sums, differences, unary signs, multiplication by a voltage-independent scalar and division by a nonzero voltage-independent scalar. A voltage reference shall preserve V(P)-V(N) polarity. Preparation shall bound source length, recursion, expression work and distinct voltage terms, and return no partial coefficients on refusal. Conditions, runtime identifiers, current references, nonlinear products/divisors, opaque parameters and unqualified quoted node semantics shall remain explicit refusals.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: Grammar/SpiceLexer.g4 SemanticHeaderOnly flag and Grammar/SpiceParser.g4 behaviorHeaderProfile reuse generated recognition for composite headers; default deck recognition leaves the flag false. BehavioralSourceSyntax.cs retains typed metadata. AffineVoltageExpressionEvaluator.cs derives only the existing generated AST and delegates constant subtrees to ParameterEvaluator. BehavioralSourceLowering.cs prepares the typed relation; parent bridge integration emits existing typed elements rather than introducing a native expression runtime.
Limits: 4096 expression UTF-16 characters, 1024 evaluated affine nodes, depth 64, default 16 distinct non-ground node terms (public evaluator supports explicit 1..64 term limits). Coefficients and offsets must remain finite. Coefficient units are output-quantity units per volt; offset units follow voltage/current quantity. Input controls remain high impedance under the existing controlled-source contract.
Verification: AffineBehaviorTests includes fixed negative cases, lexical instance overrides, physical continuation ranges, term/depth budgets and an explicit 128-case FsCheck campaign with Rnd seed 20261103. Initial helper qualification used independently built typed requests. Integrated AffineBehaviorOracleIntegration now executes OperatingPointSelection/TransientSelection through the generated managed client and compares original B voltage/current/constant cards on LU/faer in DC, complex AC and ramp transient; 78 voltage checks passed. Current polarity is independently checked through a 1 kOhm load's KCL relation. PreparationNativeOracle also checks original B cards through the full bridge. No generic nonlinear expression support or complete original control-program execution is claimed.
<<<
